1
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,440
It's from Kuroi!

2
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:39,177
There's always a chance
the worst could happen.

3
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,137
Go on ahead, you're faster than me!

4
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,200
Just hurry and catch up to Riko.

5
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,837
I'm sorry, this was my mistake.

6
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:49,840
Seriously?

7
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:53,225
I don't think this can
even count as a mistake.

8
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:56,697
I underestimated how much our
enemies would value Kuroi.

9
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:01,074
Their next move will probably be
offering to arrange an exchange for her.

10
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,637
Something like trading Amanai for Kuroi.

11
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:06,838
Or saying they'll kill Kuroi
if we don't kill Amanai.

12
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:11,442
But we have the leverage in any
negotiation, since we have Amanai.

13
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:16,945
As long as they set up the location for
the deal, we can make it work out for us.

14
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,797
I'm taking Amanai back to
Jujutsu High immediately.

15
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,457
We can have Shoko or someone
stand in as her body doll.

16
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,370
Hold on!

17
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,137
I'm going to be part of this deal too!

18
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,817
I still can't trust you two yet.

19
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:28,730
Huh?

20
00:01:28,813 --> 00:01:31,077
You're still saying
that after all of this?

21
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,395
Even if you save her?

22
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:37,847
Even if you save her, what if Kuroi isn't
back before I assimilate with Tengen?

23
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:39,838
You mean I haven't?

24
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,874
I haven't even said goodbye to her yet.

25
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,926
The kidnapper will reach
out to us eventually.

26
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:02,660
But if we realize they're
smarter than we expected,

27
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:07,605
or it turns out that bringing you will
only lessen Kuroi's chances of survival...

28
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,235
...and we'll have to leave you behind.

29
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,230
Right.

30
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,840
That works.

31
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:29,213
On the other hand, if you get scared
part way through and want to go home,

32
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,634
we'll just ignore you.

33
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,320
So keep that in mind.

34
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,537
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh,

35
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:24,620
oh.

36
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,680
Thank you.

37
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,951
I can't believe I got captured
by the Star Religious Group.

38
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,981
And worse yet, by a non-sorcerer.

39
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,965
I'm just so ashamed of myself.

40
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:38,917
You couldn't help it if they
caught you off guard like that.

41
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,118
Part of the blame lies with me, too.

42
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,300
Was I really caught off guard?

43
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:49,460
I thought I was on high alert
after the incident with Q.

44
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:52,950
Could I?

45
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:57,435
I still don't have much
recollection of being attacked.

46
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:00,200
And you all came here by plane?

47
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,480
Were you okay?

48
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,275
You weren't attacked?

49
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,221
Satoru had some good eyes on him.

50
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:11,464
Before we took off, he checked
over all the passengers and staff.

51
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:14,409
As well as inside and
outside of the plane.

52
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:19,420
And while we were in the air, I had
my cursed spirit keep watch outside.

53
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,420
It was safer than traveling by land.

54
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:27,057
But what I'm curious
about is why they chose

55
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,611
Okinawa as the place to make the exchange.

56
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:32,016
Probably to buy time, I would assume.

57
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,304
Even if they fail to kill Riko,

58
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:37,077
they could keep her from making
tomorrow's full moon deadline.

59
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,377
If that were the goal,

60
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:42,217
they would just choose a rural area
with poor transit infrastructure.

61
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,457
Maybe their plan is to take over
the airport and trap us here.

62
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:48,422
That's a possibility, but
we're going to be fine.

63
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,073
We're not the only ones here in Okinawa.

64
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:57,857
Clearly, this mission is far too
difficult for a first-year student.

65
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,587
I'm totally psyched, though.

66
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,311
I can't wait to show off in front of Code.

67
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:03,490
You know what?

68
00:06:03,573 --> 00:06:05,857
I heard that the
upperclassmen are all worn

69
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:08,177
to the bone trying to
protect one lone girl.

70
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:11,554
This is our chance to show
them we've got what it takes.

71
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:16,504
If a typhoon rolls in and shuts down the
airports, our efforts will be for naught.

72
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,000
It's a sea cucumber!

73
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:20,370
Gross!

74
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:21,900
Oh, it's so gross!

75
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:25,891
Should we really be vacationing like this?

76
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,220
Satoru's the one who suggested it.

77
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,869
He's probably showing consideration
for Riko in his own way.

78
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,904
Though we should all get going.

79
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,520
Satoru, it's time!

80
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,335
Yo, I didn't realize it was that late.

81
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,510
Hmm.

82
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,622
Suguru, let's head back
tomorrow morning instead.

83
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,120
